"FMT_WMMA_AB_16X16_BF16":["WMMA multiplicand matrix (A or B) with 16-bit brain float values.\n\nWMMA AB matrices are 16x16 and the individual elements are packed; each VGPR lane can contain 2 16-bit elements, 4 8-bit elements or 8 4-bit elements. OPSEL is ignored for AB matrices. WMMA requires the AB matrix be replicated; 2 copies of the matrix are required for wave32 mode and 4 copies are required for wave64 mode. The total number of VGPRs is the same regardless of wave size.","float"],
"FMT_WMMA_AB_16X16_F16":["WMMA multiplicand matrix (A or B) with 16-bit float values.\n\nWMMA AB matrices are 16x16 and the individual elements are packed; each VGPR lane can contain 2 16-bit elements, 4 8-bit elements or 8 4-bit elements. OPSEL is ignored for AB matrices. WMMA requires the AB matrix be replicated; 2 copies of the matrix are required for wave32 mode and 4 copies are required for wave64 mode. The total number of VGPRs is the same regardless of wave size.","float"],
"FMT_WMMA_AB_16X16_IU4":["WMMA multiplicand matrix (A or B) with 4-bit integers whose signedness is determined by the NEG modifier.\n\nWMMA AB matrices are 16x16 and the individual elements are packed; each VGPR lane can contain 2 16-bit elements, 4 8-bit elements or 8 4-bit elements. OPSEL is ignored for AB matrices. WMMA requires the AB matrix be replicated; 2 copies of the matrix are required for wave32 mode and 4 copies are required for wave64 mode. The total number of VGPRs is the same regardless of wave size.","integer"],
"FMT_WMMA_AB_16X16_IU8":["WMMA multiplicand matrix (A or B) with 8-bit integers whose signedness is determined by the NEG modifier.\n\nWMMA AB matrices are 16x16 and the individual elements are packed; each VGPR lane can contain 2 16-bit elements, 4 8-bit elements or 8 4-bit elements. OPSEL is ignored for AB matrices. WMMA requires the AB matrix be replicated; 2 copies of the matrix are required for wave32 mode and 4 copies are required for wave64 mode. The total number of VGPRs is the same regardless of wave size.","integer"],
"FMT_WMMA_DC_16X16_BF16":["WMMA destination (D) or accumulator (C) matrix with 16-bit brain float values.\n\nWMMA DC matrices are 16x16 and the individual elements are unpacked; each VGPR lane contains exactly one element. For 16-bit data OPSEL may be used to specify whether the element comes from the low or high half of the VGPR. The total number of VGPRs required depends on the wave size.","float"],
"FMT_WMMA_DC_16X16_F16":["WMMA destination (D) or accumulator (C) matrix with 16-bit float values.\n\nWMMA DC matrices are 16x16 and the individual elements are unpacked; each VGPR lane contains exactly one element. For 16-bit data OPSEL may be used to specify whether the element comes from the low or high half of the VGPR. The total number of VGPRs required depends on the wave size.","float"],
"FMT_WMMA_DC_16X16_F32":["WMMA destination (D) or accumulator (C) matrix with single precision float values.\n\nWMMA DC matrices are 16x16 and the individual elements are unpacked; each VGPR lane contains exactly one element. For 16-bit data OPSEL may be used to specify whether the element comes from the low or high half of the VGPR. The total number of VGPRs required depends on the wave size.","float"],
"FMT_WMMA_DC_16X16_I32":["WMMA destination (D) or accumulator (C) matrix with 32-bit signed integer values.\n\nWMMA DC matrices are 16x16 and the individual elements are unpacked; each VGPR lane contains exactly one element. For 16-bit data OPSEL may be used to specify whether the element comes from the low or high half of the VGPR. The total number of VGPRs required depends on the wave size.","integer"]
