"groups":{
"SALU":["Scalar ALU","Scalar ALU (SALU) instructions operate on values that are common to all work-items in the wave. These operations consist of 32-bit integer or floating-point arithmetic, and 32 or 64-bit bitwise operations, and they store results in scalar registers."],
"SMEM":["Scalar Memory","Scalar Memory (SMEM) instructions allow a shader program to load data from memory into scalar registers, making the data accessible to all work-items in the wave."],
"VALU":["Vector ALU","Vector ALU (VALU) instructions perform arithmetic or logical operations on data for each of the wave's work-item and write results back to vector registers, scalar registers or the EXEC mask."],
"VMEM":["Vector Memory","Vector-memory (VMEM) instructions transfer data to and from vector registers, making the data uniquely available for each work-item in the wave."],
"EXPORT":["Export","Export instructions copy data from a VGPR to one of the export buffers (position, color, or Z)."],
"BRANCH":["Branch","Branch instructions allow programs to jump - direct or indirect - to an instruction to be executed next, conditionally or unconditionally."],
"MESSAGE":["Message","Message instructions send a message to fixed function hardware or the host and can be used to request that a value be returned to the wave."],
"WAVE_CONTROL":["Wave Control","Wave control instructions control a wave's execution these include dependency, delay, scheduling, and wave termination operations."],
"TRAP":["Trap","Trap instructions transition into and out of the wave's trap handler"]
},
